# BoopBox broker ACLs. ACLs live entirely here, never in the app.
#
# Account model:
#   - One server account (username below; replace the placeholder to match the
#     account you create with mosquitto_passwd and BOOPBOX_MQTT_USERNAME).
#   - One account per box, whose username IS its device id (%u). A box named
#     "boop-test" authenticates as user "boop-test".
#
# Topic contract (must match app/mqtt/publish.py + app/mqtt/service.py):
#   box  pub : boopbox/<id>/boop, boopbox/<id>/version
#   box  sub : boopbox/<id>/{play,error,cmd}, boopbox/all/cmd (read-only)
#   srv  pub : boopbox/<id>/{play,error,cmd}, boopbox/all/cmd
#   srv  sub : boopbox/+/boop, boopbox/+/version

# --- Server account ---------------------------------------------------------
# Replace "boopbox-server" with the real server username (BOOPBOX_MQTT_USERNAME).
# Broad read/write across the whole tree: it talks to every device and owns the
# broadcast publish.
user boopbox-server
topic readwrite boopbox/#

# --- Per-device boxes -------------------------------------------------------
# A box is confined to its own subtree boopbox/%u/#. Split by direction so a box
# can only publish its own boop/version and only read its own play/error/cmd.
# The publish restriction is the security priority: without it a leaked box
# credential could inject commands to other devices or the cmd channel.
pattern write boopbox/%u/boop
pattern write boopbox/%u/version
pattern read boopbox/%u/play
pattern read boopbox/%u/error
pattern read boopbox/%u/cmd

# --- Broadcast exception ----------------------------------------------------
# boopbox/all/cmd sits outside every box's boopbox/<id>/# subtree, so it needs
# an explicit rule: any box may SUBSCRIBE (read) it; only the server account
# (above, via boopbox/#) may PUBLISH there.
#
# This pattern is intentionally fixed (no %u): it grants read to every
# authenticated pattern client. Mosquitto logs a "does not contain '%c' or
# '%u'" warning for it — expected and benign, not a misconfiguration.
pattern read boopbox/all/cmd
